  "explanation": "FR-010 makes shapely load on FIRST USE instead of at module import, so the first seed of a process now pays that import inside its timed region. The cost lands in ONE stage on ONE seed: seed 4 field, +0.08 to +0.10s across four independent -end bookends, and it is the only stage anywhere whose delta keeps its sign between runs - every other mover flips, which is noise. field is the paddy-fan stage (waterfields/comb.py and seams/), the geometry that loads shapely; the only other shapely stage, homesteads, is 0.08s and too small to hide it. Magnitude checks: a cold shapely.geometry + shapely.ops import measures 0.14 to 0.24s on this machine depending on cache warmth, against an observed +0.09s net of the same stage running 0.04-0.14s FASTER on the other three seeds. It is one-time per process, not per map: seeds 25, 39 and 47 are -4.0, -8.0 and -2.8 percent and the TOTAL is -3.1 percent. Nothing algorithmic changed - the geometry diff is removed module-level imports, a TYPE_CHECKING block, a loader and its call sites. Two alternatives were ruled out BY MEASUREMENT rather than argument: an inline sentinel at each call site left the slow seed unchanged and cost the 100pc floor, so it was reverted; and the per-call cost is invisible even on seed 47, the heaviest geometry in the set, whose field stage went DOWN on every bookend.",
